From ec59f0aa7596a7315c78e3767f378503a46d0fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:23:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 57/94] iio: common: qcom_smgr: no sensor reports while the AP
 is suspended

A streaming sensor kept sending reports through s2idle and woke the AP
for each one. As the stock sensors HAL does for non-wakeup sensors,
ask SMGR not to send indications during suspend in every ADD
(notify-suspend, proc_type APPS), and remove the report of every
streaming sensor from a PM notifier before the smp2p "sleepstate"
notifier says the AP sleeps, adding it back after that says the AP is
awake again, so that SMGR only gets requests from an awake AP. The IIO
buffers stay enabled. A second notifier that runs last notices an
aborted suspend, in which it would not hear PM_POST_SUSPEND.

A mutex serialises the buffering requests with the streaming and
suspend state: a buffer enable or disable while suspended only marks the
sensor, and a rate written then is used by the resume.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
